Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), perl (>= 5.40)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-audit
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         homelab-common,
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         libmojo-pg-perl,
         adduser,
         sudo
Recommends: homelab-api
Description: System-wide audit trail consumer for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Drains audit.queue (a durable staging table every other homelab-*
 service INSERTs into directly, via a narrow INSERT-only Postgres grant
 -- see Homelab::Common::AuditClient) into the real, normalized,
 partitioned audit.entries fact table, and serves the site_admin/
 audit.view-gated query endpoint fronted by homelab-api's
 /api/v1/audit/* gateway route. This service never sits on the write
 path -- producers enqueue via a local, synchronous Postgres INSERT, no
 network hop and no dependency on this service being up; if it's down,
 queued rows simply accumulate until it's back, nothing is lost.
